  "id": "associative-strength",
  "term": "associative strength",
  "definition": "Associative strength is the learned pull a stimulus has because of its history of reinforcement versus non-reinforcement. In transitive inference tasks, it refers to choosing based on how often each stimulus has been rewarded rather than on a mentally inferred order or hierarchy.",
